From bb5b2aef292c0d62c6d21589857c1f6c1f447220 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: proshiv85-byte <proshiv85@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:06:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] WIP: Exynos8895 DECON-F scanout driver for exynosdrm

Takes over the display path the bootloader sets up (DECON-F in MIPI
command mode with TE trigger, DSC, DSI, S6E3HA6 panel) and scans out
DRM framebuffers through the IDMA channel of the default window, latched
by the DECON shadow update at the next frame start. Named "exynos", so
Mesa's kmsro pairs it with panfrost for zero-copy scanout.

exynos_drm_gem: accept non-contiguous dma-buf imports (compositors
import every client buffer to check it), refuse them at framebuffer
creation instead, together with buffers above 4 GiB that the display
DMA can't reach. The DECON gets a 64-bit streaming mask so imports are
never bounced.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
